    fix(guard): exempt the tracked .env.example from the credential-store path class (OB-JUDGE-001)
    
    The tier-1 secrets step started FAILing on `.env.example` — "SENSITIVE PATH
    (credential-store path class)" — in the whole-workdir judge scan, which forced
    an overall verdict FAIL on top of a tier-2 PASS for every task. The file is
    tracked, unchanged since 2026-09-29, holds placeholder values only, and appears
    in neither commit.patch nor worktree.patch, i.e. it is not part of any change
    under review. Verdicts from 2026-10-13/15/17 record the same step passing, so
    the change is on the scanner side (gitreins REVIEW-GITREINS-027 added the path
    class), not in this repo.
    
    Add the repo-owner override the class documents: guards.sensitive_paths.allow
    with exactly one entry, ".env.example". The override covers the PATH class
    only — the content scan still runs over the file, and grep-continuous content
    findings are unaffected. It can never be silent: gitreins prints
    "sensitive-path override applied: <path>" whenever the override is used.
    
    Verified:
    - `gitreins judge --ephemeral --title repro --criterion c --skip-tier2`
      -> "Stage tier1: FAIL" with a failed secrets step (before the change)
    - same command after the change -> "Stage tier1: PASS", secrets step executed
      and passing
    - .env.example itself is untouched (git status clean for it)
    
    Board: OB-JUDGE-001.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
---
 .gitreins/config.yaml | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitreins/config.yaml b/.gitreins/config.yaml
index 8a8acc91..a8f784f8 100644
--- a/.gitreins/config.yaml
+++ b/.gitreins/config.yaml
@@ -7,6 +7,21 @@ guards:
   # made the pre-commit hook exit 1 and blocked the sync commit. Accept skips
   # on zero-work runs (they are explicit in the guard output).
   allow_skips: true
+  # OB-JUDGE-001: repo-owner override for the credential-store PATH class
+  # (gitreins REVIEW-GITREINS-027). `.env.example` is a TRACKED TEMPLATE that
+  # documents which variables the service reads — it holds placeholder values
+  # only, is not a credential store, and is not part of any change under
+  # review. Without this override the tier-1 secrets step FAILs on it in the
+  # whole-workdir judge scan (the file appears in neither commit.patch nor
+  # worktree.patch), forcing overall verdict FAIL on top of a tier-2 PASS.
+  # This override suppresses the PATH-CLASS finding only for this exact
+  # filename; content findings are unaffected and every pass that uses the
+  # override is printed as "sensitive-path override applied: <path>" — the
+  # suppression can never be silent. Do NOT add globs that could cover a real
+  # credential file (.env, .env.local, *.pem, *.key).
+  sensitive_paths:
+    allow:
+      - ".env.example"
   go:
     build: true
     # lint: DISABLED 2026-10-04 (OB-GAP-086 board row). gitreins 0.15.0's
